(ned -- C ZERO DETECTION, operator spec 2026-08-03. A is taken AS GIVEN.)
(GEOMETRY. Tilting A by +-45 swings the tool tip horizontally. At true C zero)
(that swing is pure Y, so a probe driven toward the puck in +X contacts at the)
(SAME X for both tilts. A C error phi rotates the swing and puts an X)
(component into it that FLIPS sign between -45 and +45, so:)
(     dX = -2 * dy * sin phi)
(where dy is the tip's sideways offset off centre -- because putting the tip)
(on the puck makes that offset exactly the swing. So the SETUP supplies the)
(scale factor and no arm length is needed:)
(     phi = asin of [-dX / 2dy])

(TEACH ONCE, THEN REPLAY. LinuxCNC cannot be jogged mid-program and the 5x)
(A-C iteration cannot stop to ask, so the pose is taught by a separate)
(button: the operator jogs A to -45 and the tip into place, presses SET C)
(REF, and cal_c_ref.ngc stores it as offsets from the puck centre -- #3058)
(dy, #3060 depth below top, #3061 X offset. Every run here replays those.)

(SCOPE NOTE: named parameters are LOCAL to the subroutine that assigns them,)
(and subroutine definitions do not nest. The probe helper is therefore a)
(FILE-level sub taking its tilt and Y offset positionally, reading the rest)
(from GLOBAL _cc_ parameters, and returning the touch X in #<_cc_tx>.)

(THE REFERENCE IS XYZ, AND Y IS TIED TO THE TILT SIGN.)
(  #3061 X offset -- in FRONT of centre, the standoff the probe drives from)
(  #3058 Y offset -- where the -45 roll puts the tip; the +45 pass MIRRORS it)
(                    to -#3058, because rolling the other way throws the tip)
(                    to the other side of centre by the same amount)
(  #3060 depth     -- below the top, the SAME for both passes)
(Get the Y mirror wrong and the two passes probe different points on the)
(puck, which is no longer a C measurement at all.)

(Results: #3055 = dX before, #3056 = dX after, #3057 = C correction applied.)
(A is tilted +-45 about #3069, the accumulated A correction -- NOT about the)
(stale DRO zero, or every StartA would be undone on the next StartC. #3070)
(accumulates C the same way. Both routines park at that pose so switching)
(between A and C always starts from the same place.)

(============================== main cycle =================================)
o<cal_c_zero> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  #<safe>  = 5.0        (operator 2026-08-03: 5 mm for every cal routine)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL C: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL C: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (--- capture the reference HERE if SET C REF is waiting on a jog ---------)
  (One button, one job: SET C REF positions, THIS records. Operator)
  (2026-08-03. Once stored, every later run -- including StartAC -- replays)
  (the offsets with no operator input.)
  o10 if [#3059 EQ 1]
    #<a_now> = #5423
    o11 if [ABS[#<a_now> - [#3069 - 45]] GT 5.0]
      #3059 = 0
      (abort, CAL C: A is at #<a_now> deg, not 45 below its calibrated zero. Press SET C REF again.)
    o11 endif
    #<dx_off> = [#5420 - #<cx>]
    #<dy_off> = [#5421 - #<cy>]
    #<depth>  = [#<top> - #5422]
    o12 if [ABS[#<dy_off>] LT 1.0]
      (abort, CAL C: the tip is within 1 mm of centre in Y. That offset IS the scale factor of the C measurement so it cannot be near zero - jog sideways as the -45 tilt puts it.)
    o12 endif
    o13 if [#<depth> LE 0]
      (abort, CAL C: the tip is at or above the puck top - jog DOWN so that driving toward centre would strike the puck.)
    o13 endif
    o14 if [#<dx_off> GE 0]
      (abort, CAL C: the tip is not in FRONT of the puck - it must sit at negative X of centre so the probe drives toward centre in +X.)
    o14 endif
    #3061 = #<dx_off>
    #3058 = #<dy_off>
    #3060 = #<depth>
    #3059 = 0
    (PRINT, CAL C: reference captured from your jog - X offset #3061 mm, dy off centre #3058 mm, depth below top #3060 mm.)
  o10 else
    o15 if [#3058 EQ 0]
      (abort, CAL C: no C reference. Press SET C REF, jog the tip into place, then press StartC.)
    o15 endif
  o10 endif

  (--- shared setup, GLOBAL so the file-level helper can read it -----------)
  #<_cc_cy>    = #<cy>
  #<_cc_top>   = #<top>
  #<_cc_xr>    = [#<cx> + #3061]
  #<_cc_zoff>  = #3060
  #<_cc_safe>  = #<safe>
  #<_cc_reach> = 30.0    (max +X probe travel from the taught standoff)
  #<_cc_fpr>   = 100.0
  #<_cc_fla>   = 10.0
  #<_cc_ftr>   = 500.0
  #<_cc_fck>   = 200.0
  #<_cc_back>  = 1.0     (backoff before the latch, 1 mm is plenty)

  #<dy> = #3058

  M50 P0
  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5

  (=== BEFORE: -45 at the taught Y, then +45 at the mirrored Y ============)
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 - 45]] [#<dy>]
  #<x_neg_b> = #<_cc_tx>
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 + 45]] [0 - #<dy>]
  #<x_pos_b> = #<_cc_tx>
  #<dx_b> = [#<x_pos_b> - #<x_neg_b>]
  #3055 = #<dx_b>
  (PRINT, CAL C BEFORE: x at -45 = #<x_neg_b>, x at +45 = #<x_pos_b>, DELTA X = #<dx_b>)

  (=== correct: phi = asin of [-dX / 2dy] =================================)
  (dy KEEPS ITS SIGN. dX = -2 * dy * sin phi, so dy must enter signed:)
  (with ABS, a jog to NEGATIVE dy flipped phi and C rotated the wrong way by)
  (the full amount, doubling the error instead of removing it. The recheck)
  (would have caught it, but only after swinging the head the wrong way.)
  (Found by inspection 2026-08-03, never run on the machine.)
  #<ratio> = [[0 - #<dx_b>] / [2 * #<dy>]]
  o220 if [ABS[#<ratio>] GE 1.0]
    G90
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: dX exceeds twice the taught offset - the geometry does not fit the model, refusing to rotate C.)
  o220 endif
  #<phi> = ASIN[#<ratio>]
  #3057 = #<phi>
  (PRINT, CAL C: rotating C by #<phi> deg)

  o230 if [ABS[#<phi>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL C: computed correction over 5 deg - refusing to swing the head that far on one measurement)
  o230 endif

  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G91
  G1 C#<phi> F600
  G90
  #3070 = [#3070 + #<phi>]

  (=== AFTER: the same pair again =========================================)
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 - 45]] [#<dy>]
  #<x_neg_a> = #<_cc_tx>
  o<cc_probe> call [[#3069 + 45]] [0 - #<dy>]
  #<x_pos_a> = #<_cc_tx>
  #<dx_a> = [#<x_pos_a> - #<x_neg_a>]
  #3056 = #<dx_a>
  (PRINT, CAL C AFTER: x at -45 = #<x_neg_a>, x at +45 = #<x_pos_a>, DELTA X = #<dx_a>)

  (=== park + verdict =====================================================)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F[#<_cc_ftr>]
  M65 P3
  M50 P1

  o240 if [ABS[#<dx_a>] LT ABS[#<dx_b>]]
    (PRINT, CAL C OK: DELTA X #<dx_b> -> #<dx_a> mm, C moved #<phi> deg. Sign is correct.)
    (DEBUG, CAL C: dX before #<dx_b>, after #<dx_a>, C corrected #<phi> deg)
  o240 else
    (DEBUG, CAL C FAILED: dX before #<dx_b>, after #<dx_a> - got WORSE. Flip the phi sign.)
    (abort, CAL C: correction made it WORSE - dX #<dx_b> then #<dx_a>. The math or the sign is wrong. Failing loudly by design.)
  o240 endif

o<cal_c_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
